  "function": {
    "uniprot_function": "Ligand for members of the frizzled family of seven transmembrane receptors. Functions in the canonical Wnt signaling pathway that results in activation of transcription factors of the TCF/LEF family. Component of the Wnt-Fzd-LRP5-LRP6 signaling complex. Required for paraxial mesoderm formation, somite and tailbud development in embryonic development.",
    "catalytic_activity": null,
    "subcellular_location": [
      "Endoplasmic reticulum",
      "Golgi apparatus",
      "Trans-Golgi network",
      "Plasma membrane",
      "Extracellular space",
      "Extracellular vesicles"
    ],
    "tissue_specificity": "Expressed in developing neural tube (roof plate, dorsal spinal cord), developing brain (narrow midline region extending into telencephalon), paraxial mesoderm, periumbilical mesenchyme. NOT expressed in limb ectoderm (unlike WNT3). Wnt3a null mutants lack paraxial mesoderm and have tailbud defects.",
