    "pathway_role_summary": "WNT3A is a canonical Wnt ligand that activates Wnt/beta-catenin signaling. After PORCN-mediated dual lipidation (Cys77, Ser209) in ER, WNT3A binds WLS for secretion. Extracellular WNT3A binds FZD receptors and LRP5/6 co-receptors forming ternary signaling complex. This recruits DVL, sequesters AXIN from destruction complex, redirects GSK3B to phosphorylate LRP6 (not CTNNB1), stabilizes beta-catenin, enabling nuclear translocation and TCF/LEF-dependent transcription. Essential for paraxial mesoderm formation, somitogenesis, and neural tube patterning in development."
  },
