      "disease": "Tetra-amelia syndrome (WNT3, not WNT3A)",
      "omim_id": "273395",
      "mutation_type": "Germline",
      "description": "WNT3 (close homolog) Q83X homozygous nonsense mutation causes tetra-amelia with craniofacial and urogenital defects. WNT3A itself not associated with disease, suggesting potential embryonic lethality or functional redundancy."
    }
