    "data_quality_notes": "Comprehensive high-quality dataset. Cryo-EM structures: 7DRT (2.2 Å, WNT3A-WLS), 7URD (2.92 Å, PORCN-WNT3A peptide-LGK974). Lipidation sites (Cys77, Ser209) extensively characterized with clear functional distinctions. Quantitative binding affinities available for 7 FZD receptors (Kd range 2.3-29.9 nM kinetic, 4.9-48.6 nM saturation) from live-cell NanoBiT/BRET assays. WNT3A-LRP6 affinity: 174 nM (E3E4 alone), 9 nM (full E1E4). Site-specific binding information from mutagenesis and structural studies. Unique IDs assigned to all domains, motifs, PTMs, and interactions to enable unambiguous reference in rule-based models. N-glycosylation sites predicted from WNT3 homology (experimental validation for WNT3A pending). Kinetic parameters for PORCN enzymatic activity not available in literature.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "WNT3A is ideal for modeling canonical Wnt pathway with following features: (1) Dual lipidation checkpoint: Ser209 palmitoleoylation (secretion-enabling via WLS) vs Cys77 palmitoylation (receptor-binding-enabling). (2) Quantitative FZD receptor binding affinities (2.3-29.9 nM) enable parametrization of receptor selectivity and competition. (3) Site-specific binding interfaces: thumb (lipid site 1) and index finger (protein site 2) engaging FZD CRD. (4) Ternary complex stoichiometry: WNT3A bridges FZD-LRP6 with E3E4 domain preference. (5) Biogenesis pathway: ER synthesis → PORCN dual lipidation → WLS cargo loading → secretion. (6) Druggable nodes: PORCN inhibitors (LGK974 clinical stage, IWP-2). (7) High-resolution structures (7DRT at 2.2 Å) enable molecular-level modeling. (8) Unique identifiers for all features enable precise rule specification in Kappa models."
